{
  "_readme": {
    "what": "Every structure's spawn rate, in one file. A GROUP is one shared structure_set (creativeengineering:group/<name>) holding every structure in the structure tag group/<name> (structure_tags.json): all members share its grid, so no two of them ever start closer than its separation, whatever mod they come from. Every structure that is in no group keeps its own set and is tuned under \"standalone\". Rejoin the world to apply (new chunks only); structure_tag_report.md shows what the game applied.",
    "group placement": "spacing: one grid slot per spacing x spacing chunks (the group's top density). separation: minimum chunks between any two members. salt: which grid (leave it). Optional: spread_type, frequency (chance per slot for the whole group), locate_offset, exclusion_zone {other_set, chunk_count} (keep off another set's grid slots; it checks slots, not real structures, so keep chunk_count small).",
    "per structure": "weight: who wins a slot where several members can spawn (relative, whole numbers). frequency: 0..1, chance that the winner really spawns; otherwise the slot stays empty, so lowering one never makes another more common. enabled: false removes it. Where a structure is the only member that fits the biome, it gets every slot x its frequency.",
    "standalone": "Keyed by the structure_set id in structure_config.json. placement: only the fields you change (spacing, separation, frequency, count, locate_offset...; the rest come from \"original\" in structure_config.json). structures: frequency / enabled / optional weight, same meaning as in a group.",
    "moving a structure": "Edit the group/* tags in structure_tags.json, then run python3 tools/gen_structure_groups.py: it adds the new member with a weight and frequency fitted to its mod default and leaves everything else alone. A tagged member with no entry here still works (the game fills in a rough default and flags it).",
    "estimates": "python3 tools/gen_structure_groups.py --check rewrites structure_group_estimates.md: expected structures per area for every structure, from its real biome areas."
  },
